\title{Test: rasterised datasets}
\description{
Flags every record of a dataset whose coordinates lie on a regular grid, as
when records were collected or published per grid cell. For each axis the
absolute coordinates are binned into about 3000 classes, the
autocorrelation of the bin counts is computed, and its outliers (values
above Q75 + \code{T1} x IQR in sliding windows) are located; regularly spaced
outliers, at a common distance between \code{reg_dist_min} and \code{reg_dist_max}
degrees found at least \code{reg_out_thresh} times, mark the axis as periodic.
A dataset fails when both axes are periodic (\code{axis = "both"}) or the chosen
one is. Datasets with fewer than \code{min_unique_ds_size} distinct coordinates
are not tested.
}
